Q7: How would Madison's perception of Granite City been different if he had not have met Professor Parnell?
  A. His perception of Granite City would have been misconstrued because he would have lacked an explanation to why the people of Granite City are the way that they are.
  B. His perception would have been unchanged because he would have figured out that Granite City was making false insurance claims on his own.
  C. His perception of Granite City would have been much more positive without Professor Parnell's explanation of the city's grim secret. 
  D. His perception of Granite City would have stayed the same; however, he would have figured out the situation in Granite City much more quickly without Professor Parnell..
  Gold answer: A (1)

Q8: Why did Madison investigate the manual record files prior to visiting Granite City?
